# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Study Tracker — copy to .env.local and fill in what you need.
# Everything here is optional; the app runs with none of it set.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where your database and uploaded files live.
# Point this at a synced folder (Dropbox, iCloud) to use it on two machines.
# STUDY_DATA_DIR=/Users/you/Documents/study-tracker-data

# Swap SQLite for Turso/libSQL in the cloud without touching any code.
# DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-db.turso.io
# DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=

# --- LeetCode -------------------------------------------------------------
# Your public username is enough for: solved counts by difficulty, per-topic
# counts, the submission calendar, and your ~20 most recent solves.
# You can also just set this in Setup in the UI instead of here.
# LEETCODE_USERNAME=

# To import your COMPLETE solved history, the app has to talk to LeetCode as
# you. This is your own session cookie for your own account. It stays in this
# file and in your local database, and is only ever sent to leetcode.com.
#
# How to get it:
#   1. Sign in to leetcode.com in your browser
#   2. DevTools -> Application -> Cookies -> https://leetcode.com
#   3. Copy the VALUE of LEETCODE_SESSION, and of csrftoken
#
# It expires every month or so. When it does the app falls back to public mode
# and says so in Setup — re-paste the value to resume full sync.
# LEETCODE_SESSION=
# LEETCODE_CSRF=
